Package: blindspot
Title: Bayesian Spatiotemporal Surveillance Quality Monitoring
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    c(person(
        given = "Mohamed",
        family = "Yusuf",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "truenomad@who.int",
        comment = c(ORCID = "XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX")
    ))
Description: Estimates district-level expected case detection
    rates using Bayesian spatiotemporal models (BYM2 via INLA),
    adjusts for reporting delays, monitors temporal trends via
    first-order random walk smoothing, detects acute surveillance
    disruptions via Bayesian online changepoint detection, and
    classifies surveillance quality into operational response
    categories. The core output is a surveillance performance
    index (SPI) defined as the ratio of delay-adjusted observed
    counts to model-estimated expected counts, with full
    posterior uncertainty quantification. The SPI adapts the
    standardised morbidity ratio (SMR) framework from disease
    mapping to surveillance process monitoring. Designed for
    acute flaccid paralysis (AFP) surveillance in the polio
    endgame but applicable to any case-based disease surveillance
    system with spatially distributed reporting units and count
    data, including measles discard surveillance, neonatal
    tetanus reporting, and DHIS2 completeness monitoring.
